Package: statcram
Type: Package
Title: Exam-Friendly Statistics Toolkit with a Numbered Menu
Version: 0.8.8
Authors@R: person("OpenAI","Prototype",email="noreply@example.com",role=c("aut","cre"))
Description: An offline statistics exam toolkit. A numbered menu (sc()) and
    consistently named functions cover descriptive statistics, probability,
    confidence intervals, hypothesis tests, power and sample size,
    chi-square tests and linear regression. Every procedure accepts raw data
    (any vector or expression, including variables created during the exam)
    or the summary numbers given in the question, and prints the formulas
    with the numbers plugged in, the decision, exam wording and the call to
    re-run it. sc_table() rebuilds tables printed on paper as data frames.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 3.6.0)
Imports: graphics, grDevices, stats, utils
Suggests: testthat (>= 3.0.0)
Config/testthat/edition: 3
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
RoxygenNote: 7.3.1
